sis of ${R}^{n}$ consisting of the eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A$ with corresponding eigenvalues \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}\\ge {\\lambda }_{2}\\ge …\\ge {\\lambda }_{n}.\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{1},$\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{2},$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nIn our example, we see that\n\n- $||A{v}_{1}||=6={\\sigma }_{1},$ which means that ${\\lambda }_{1}={6}^{2}=36,$ and\n\n- $||A{v}_{2}||=2={\\sigma }_{2},$ which means that ${\\lambda }_{2}={2}^{2}=4.$\n\nTherefore, an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=36$ of ${A}^{T}A$ is ${v}_{1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369749 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369749 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369749 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186369750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369749 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0b2343b2-0201-5c51-9b20-71321c6397b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369750 #edb/ref 1080 "{v}_{1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369750 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369750 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e5508c57-b781-54c4-ac3c-ea5f7e99fa1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369751 #edb/ref 1080 "{v}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369751 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369751 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9ad78cd4-8bf5-5788-bd3c-9fdda0f21f36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369752 #edb/ref 1080 "6{v}_{1}+2{v}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369752 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17